&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A career driven by you. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Join AutoScout24 Group and experience life in the fast lane. We’re not just leading the market; we’re creating it. We’re constantly innovating, evolving and transforming things for our customers. We’re driven, ambitious and determined to do our best work, together. For a career that doesn’t stand still, where you can put your ideas in the driving seat and change the way the world moves, join our international community.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:257}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:257}&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring two senior software engineers for Autonex Tech Effectiveness (ATE), a team within Core Tech working across business units. We build software that helps engineering teams deliver more effectively and make better use of their resources. Our remit spans cloud and AI spending, software licensing, delivery insights, and the workflows that connect them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll build AI agents, integrations, and internal products that turn data into useful decisions and actions. You’ll work closely with engineers, engineering leaders, and Finance to understand real problems, ship solutions, and measure their impact. We’re looking for a strong software engineer who is excited about agentic AI and cares about how engineering organizations work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See what this looks like in practice:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://tech.autoscout24.com/blog/posts/ai-teammates-nex-and-fyn/&quot;&gt;AI Teammates for Scrum and FinOps: How AutoScout24 Built Nex and Fyn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve AI products such as Nex and Fyn, their companion tools, and self-service analytics for engineering effectiveness and FinOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design agentic workflows with tool calling, orchestration, retrieval, and memory. Make their actions predictable through clear permissions, human approvals, and auditable execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect engineering and financial data through APIs and reliable data pipelines, integrating with tools such as Slack, Jira, our developer portal, and cloud and AI providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build FinOps capabilities for cost attribution, forecasting, anomaly detection, and optimization across cloud, AI, and software spend. Keep financial calculations accurate and traceable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve delivery visibility and reduce administrative toil, waiting time, and workflow friction. Help teams understand the balance between operational work and product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own products from discovery and design through deployment and operation. Build evaluations, tests, and observability that cover agent behavior, reliability, security, latency, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering teams, Finance, Procurement, and Employee Tech to prioritize useful improvements. Use adoption, user feedback, and measurable outcomes to guide what you build next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you need to succeed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior-level software engineering experience, typically 5+ years, building and operating production applications or services, with strong skills in design, testing, debugging, and maintainable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building LLM-powered applications and agentic systems used in real workflows. You can explain the design decisions, failure modes, and trade-offs behind what you’ve built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in at least one language, ideally Python or TypeScript, and confidence working with APIs, data integrations, and distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong interest in AI and a habit of experimenting, learning, and shipping. Modern AI coding tools such as Claude Code or Codex are part of your day-to-day work, and you take responsibility for the result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience deploying and running software in AWS or a comparable cloud, including CI/CD and observability. You can make sensible choices about reliability, security, and operating cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in engineering effectiveness: developer experience, delivery flow, automation, and responsible use of resources. You want to understand whether a tool improves someone’s work and how to measure that.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication, product thinking, and ownership. You can turn an ambiguous problem into a practical solution and work with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience that would help&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FinOps, cloud cost optimization, engineering analytics, developer experience, or engineering operations. Curiosity and willingness to learn these domains matter too.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agent frameworks, MCP integrations, Amazon Bedrock, or AgentCore. Our current agents use the Strands Agents SDK; experience with other stacks is welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building internal tools, dashboards, or data products that people use to make decisions, and using metrics carefully in their context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Why this team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a small team that uses AI throughout its own work and builds products for colleagues across the business. You’ll have ownership of meaningful problems and room to shape the solutions. Success means tools people trust and use, less time lost to friction, and better decisions about engineering investment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At AutoScout24 Group, we value diverse perspectives and an inclusive, respectful working environment. If you’re excited to build agentic AI products that improve how engineering works, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A culture of growth &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;With over 50 nationalities represented, we’re proud to welcome people of all backgrounds to our growing community, and we’re always finding new ways to help people feel welcomed and included. Here, you’ll have the tools, training and support you need to work in a way that suits you, learn new skills and reach your potential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For a career where you can drive our business and shape your future, apply now.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A career driven by you. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Join AutoScout24 Group and experience life in the fast lane. We’re not just leading the market; we’re creating it. We’re constantly innovating, evolving and transforming things for our customers. We’re driven, ambitious and determined to do our best work, together. For a career that doesn’t stand still, where you can put your ideas in the driving seat and change the way the world moves, join our international community.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:257}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Fullstack Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to build and evolve products for our dealer customers. You’ll work primarily with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;React, TypeScript and Node.js&lt;/strong&gt;, with a stronger focus on frontend development while contributing across the full stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll bring strong engineering fundamentals, sound technical judgement and the ability to take ownership of features in a complex, established product environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside building customer-facing AI capabilities, you’ll use&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;GenAI tools in your everyday development work&lt;/strong&gt;. We value curiosity and a willingness to learn; your depth as a software engineer is the foundation, and we’ll support you in developing your AI skills further.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join one of our product engineering teams and build products used by our dealer customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build and evolve customer-facing applications using&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;React, TypeScript and Node.js&lt;/strong&gt;, with a stronger focus on frontend development while contributing across the full stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of features throughout the full development lifecycle — from technical design and implementation to testing, deployment and operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within large, established codebases and continuously improve their quality, maintainability and architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product, Design and other engineers to turn customer and business needs into pragmatic technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use GenAI development tools to support activities such as coding, debugging, refactoring, testing and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply sound engineering judgement when using AI-generated solutions, validating outputs and ensuring that quality, security and maintainability remain high.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge, contribute to technical discussions and help continuously improve engineering practices within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you’ll bring:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of hands-on software engineering experience&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;building and operating production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong professional experience with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;React, TypeScript and Node.js&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong frontend engineering experience combined with the ability and willingness to contribute across backend services when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;large, existing codebases&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;and delivering maintainable, well-tested software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software engineering fundamentals, including application architecture, testing, code quality and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking ownership of features or technical solutions from design through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to make pragmatic technical decisions and clearly explain the reasoning and trade-offs behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating effectively with Product, Design and Engineering colleagues in cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;GenAI and AI-assisted software development&lt;/strong&gt;, with an interest in incorporating these tools into your everyday engineering workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A learning mindset and the ability to quickly pick up new technologies and tools. Willingness to learn Java and contribute to Java-based backend services as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and the ability to collaborate, challenge ideas constructively and contribute to technical discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing backend services with Java.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI-assisted development tools such as GitHub Copilot, ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude or Codex.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building features or applications that integrate&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;LLMs or AI APIs&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud environments such as&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;AWS&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience building products or tools for B2B customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A culture of growth&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;With over 50 nationalities represented, we’re proud to welcome people of all backgrounds to our growing community, and we’re always finding new ways to help people feel welcomed and included. Here, you’ll have the tools, training and support you need to work in a way that suits you, learn new skills and reach your potential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For a career where you can drive our business and shape your future, apply now.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Design Director - Patient (x/f/m)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doctolib is a mission-driven healthcare technology company, founded in Paris in 2013. Today, nearly &lt;strong&gt;3,000 people&lt;/strong&gt; work across Europe to transform the way healthcare is delivered and experienced.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than &lt;strong&gt;500,000 healthcare professionals&lt;/strong&gt; use Doctolib’s solutions, and the patient app is used by approximately &lt;strong&gt;90 million people&lt;/strong&gt; across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For patients, Doctolib began as a simple way to find a healthcare professional and book an appointment. We are now building something much more ambitious: an &lt;strong&gt;AI-powered Health Companion&lt;/strong&gt; that helps people navigate care, understand their health and take the right next step throughout their health journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This means moving beyond a primarily transactional product towards an experience that supports patients before, during and after care, through access to care, health information, patient data, messaging, recommendations, care plans and AI-powered assistance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Design Director to help define what this next generation of patient experience should look and feel like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will build and lead&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Product Design Director, Patient&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the design vision and quality bar for Doctolib’s patient experience. You will report to our VP Design and work closely with the Product, Engineering, Medical, Data and Business leadership teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your scope will cover the full patient journey, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;access to care, search and booking;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;patient messaging and teleconsultation;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the Patient Health Record and patient context;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the app homepage and daily health experience;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;health content and prevention;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;recommendations, reminders and care plans;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;new patient services and subscription experiences;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;conversational and AI-powered experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The current team includes &lt;strong&gt;six Senior Product Designers and one Senior Content Designer&lt;/strong&gt;. You will lead, coach and develop this team while shaping the organisation and operating model needed to support the next phase of the Patient product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mandate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the design vision for the Patient stream, from a high-traffic booking experience to a trusted Health Companion used throughout the health journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge two equally important challenges: continuing to improve the core access-to-care experience while creating new reasons for patients to return beyond booking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the quality bar for product design, interaction design and content across the patient experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close enough to the product and the craft to make high-quality design decisions, not only set direction from a distance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape AI-native experiences that are clear, useful and trustworthy, including recommendations, conversational interfaces and next-best actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong design principles for transparency, explainability, uncertainty, user control and safe escalation in a healthcare context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a high-performing design organisation, including hiring, coaching, talent development and second-line leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create effective ways of working across Design, Product, Engineering, Medical, Data and Business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scale a coherent experience across countries, languages and different healthcare contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect design decisions to user behaviour, product outcomes and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year, you will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;established a clear and compelling design vision for the Patient stream;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;raised the quality bar across both core access-to-care journeys and newer Health Companion experiences;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;helped define a coherent interaction model for AI-powered patient experiences;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;strengthened collaboration between Design, Product, Engineering and Medical;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;developed a clear operating model and growth plan for the Patient Design organisation;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;helped Doctolib increase the value and relevance of the patient experience beyond appointment booking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are likely to bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading Product Design, 10+ years in product design including 3+ years in people leadership..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a consumer product organisation, ideally one used by millions of people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of designing and scaling products across multiple markets, with an understanding of localisation, cultural differences and the balance between global consistency and local relevance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing at least five Product Designers, ideally a larger organisation including senior individual contributors and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product design craft and creative judgement. You can recognise excellent work, make difficult quality trade-offs and stay close enough to the details to raise the standard of the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience connecting design choices to measurable outcomes such as adoption, conversion, engagement, retention, satisfaction or user behaviour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong and practical understanding of AI-native product experiences. You have thought deeply about how AI changes interaction design, user expectations, trust, transparency and control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing with uncertainty, recommendations, personalisation or conversational interfaces is highly relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to operate across complex products and stakeholders, while maintaining clarity and momentum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A concise and compelling communication style. You can articulate a clear point of view, align senior stakeholders and inspire teams to move in a new direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare or another regulated, trust-sensitive environment is valuable, but healthcare experience is not required. What matters is your respect for domain expertise and your ability to design responsibly in high-stakes contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English. French or German would be a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working style aligned with the Doctolib Playbook: User First, Medical Expertise, Forefront of Innovation, Bold, Drive, Passion, Humility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Doctolib, why now?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doctolib gives you the opportunity to work on a consumer product with significant reach, strong European scale and a mission that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The patient product already has a large and engaged audience. The next challenge is to make the experience more useful, more contextual and more present in people’s everyday health journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join at a defining moment:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Doctolib is moving from appointment booking towards continuous health support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI is becoming a core part of the product experience, not an isolated feature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Patient Design organisation is being strengthened and reshaped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The product must work across multiple European countries, languages and healthcare systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The design foundations for the next chapter are still being built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape a new category at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;consumer product design, healthcare and AI&lt;/strong&gt;, and to define how people will discover, understand and manage their health in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Doctolib is an equal opportunity employer. We believe diverse teams build better products and improve healthcare for more people. We welcome applications regardless of gender, religion, age, sexual orientation, ethnicity, disability or place of origin. If you have a disability, please let us know how we can make the recruitment process more accessible.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
